WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.420
We knew Mando's scrappy little plan was going
to go poorly, but we didn't expect it to be

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.670
quite this much of a disaster.

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:11.080
In Chapter 7 of The Mandalorian, Mando's troubles
are stacked higher than ever before.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:14.960
Titled "The Reckoning," the newest episode
of the Disney+ series proves that a reckoning

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.130
is definitely here, and its consequences have
had drastic effects on some of the show's

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:20.720
beloved characters.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.250
Turn back now if you want to avoid some mudhorn-sized
spoilers.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:28.419
Kuiil, the free Ugnaught, has fallen in his
last-ditch effort to secure the Child back

00:00:28.419 --> 00:00:30.560
at the Mandalorian's ship, the Razor Crest.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.881
Meanwhile, Mando, Cara Dune, and Greef Carga
are pinned down inside the offices of The

00:00:34.881 --> 00:00:39.930
Client in Navarro, confronting the major antagonist
we've all been waiting for: Moff Gideon, a

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.470
former governor of the Empire.

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:46.370
Oh, and The Client is also dead, shot down
by the no-nonsense Moff Gideon.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:50.300
And worst of all, The Child is in the hands
of the Empire, or what's left of it.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.000
Moff Gideon shows us he's rigged the board
from the beginning, revealing that he's tapped

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.650
Mando's communications.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:59.570
He's brought a force of Stormtroopers that
Mando can't possibly outgun, and there's no

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.899
enclave of other Mandalorians or bounty hunters
around to help him get out this time.

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:06.220
Moff Gideon is a different kind of villain.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:10.890
While The Client spoke of Baby Yoda transactionally
and as a scientific specimen, Gideon, on the

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:13.170
other hand, describes him in different terms:

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:20.130
"It means more to me than you will ever know."

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:24.380
The stakes have always been presented as high
from the very first episode of The Mandalorian,

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:26.190
but only now are they beginning to be explained.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:31.210
The Child, who has taken a backseat in most
of the Chapters so far, is using more of his

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:35.960
powers than ever before, but in this episode,
he carries out verifiable miracles with the

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:40.660
Force, and it's things we've never seen in
the canonical Star Wars universe ever before.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:44.860
We were given a hint of Baby Yoda's strength
back in Chapter 2, when Mando has that nasty

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:46.120
gash in his arm.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:50.090
Baby Yoda clambers out of his floating pram
and reaches for the wound, only to be picked

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.710
up and put back to bed.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:56.430
Now we know why for sure: Baby Yoda can heal
significant wounds with the Force.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:02:00.290
We can think of several instances across the
Skywalker saga in which that little trick

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:02.409
would have been extremely handy.

00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:05.400
It's another game-changer, and creates more
questions than answers.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:09.830
It is confirmed, however, that Mando has no
idea what the Force is.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:14.079
Kuiil doesn't know it by name, but has heard
legends and rumors, which would make sense,

00:02:14.079 --> 00:02:16.950
having been a former slave of the Empire under
Emperor Palpatine.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:21.360
Cara Dune doesn't say what she knows either
way, despite having been Force-choked seconds

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.790
before, and being a decorated, high-ranking
veteran of the Rebellion.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:27.819
Does she know more about the Force than she
wants to let on?

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:31.629
This Chapter also takes a quick moment to
shoot down at least one fan theory when Kuiil

00:02:31.629 --> 00:02:35.819
expresses doubt that Baby Yoda is a clone,
or somehow grown by synthetic means.

00:02:35.819 --> 00:02:41.220
If Baby Yoda is a genuine biological article,
where in the great, wide galaxy did he come

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.220
from?

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.939
And what's a "strand cast"?

00:02:43.939 --> 00:02:47.319
By the end of the Chapter, it appears that
Mando has completely lost.

00:02:47.319 --> 00:02:51.150
The Child is out of his possession, and he's
trapped with his only allies.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:55.310
Except for a few Jawas who were really asking
for it, Mando has been very measured in doling

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.680
out his wrath upon others.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:00.359
He often chooses not to kill, because he's
trying his best to be honorable.

00:03:00.359 --> 00:03:04.840
He is, nonetheless, pretty angry and stressed
out all the time and has learned how to contain

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:05.840
it.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.959
But what happens when Mando cares too much?

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:12.139
Many people have died because of his abrupt
impulse to be a dad, and the rising body count

00:03:12.139 --> 00:03:14.040
shows no signs of halting.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:18.199
There's a finale ahead with Chapter 8, but
it seems like it'll only bring more suffering

00:03:18.199 --> 00:03:19.709
to Mando's feet.

